      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\text{ }1\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot (-5)+5\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{67}\\sqrt{55}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}})≈{70.76}^{∘}.\n$$",
